  "notes": "Cash basis audit. Governmental: one fund (General), p1 (p5 is a duplicate copy with auditor tick marks). Beginning cash not printed (fund balances recorded); ending cash = General Fund total assets (cash at bank + county treasurer) p4. Business-type from the cash-basis proprietary statement Total column (p7); receipts total = Total operating revenues 677,730; disbursements total 583,710 printed on the Statement of Activities (p3) = operating expenses 512,193 + nonoperating debt service 71,517. The only supplementary schedule is the combined all-funds budgetary comparison (p2), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental (p1) and proprietary (p7) statements; Water and Sewer expenditure detail totals add nonoperating debt service to total operating expenses (computed). State receipts 99,120 = 63,770 Public Works operating grants + 35,350 state receipts for general purposes on p3 (not split). Balance sheet: governmental funds statement (p4, equals SoA governmental net position 397,426) plus proprietary statement of net position (p6); total net position 829,213 printed on p3. No government-wide statement of net position in the trim. Read pages 1-7 of 7"
}
